  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "Given:\n\nfrac{{2x + 3}}{{18 div 3 × 4 + 2}} = frac{{12 × 3 + 5}}{{2 × 4 div 2}}\n\nConcept used:\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/83ad200c05af7ff0a96c689e1309a38eee4e23c73e3e9636ad108a7806b6c852.png] \n\nCalculation:\n\nfrac{{2x + 3}}{{18 div 3 × 4 + 2}} = frac{{12 × 3 + 5}}{{2 × 4 div 2}}\n\n⇒ frac{{2x + 3}}{{6 × 4 + 2}} = frac{{12 × 3 + 5}}{{2 × 2}}\n\n⇒ frac{{2x + 3}}{{24 + 2}} = frac{{36 + 5}}{4}\n\n⇒ frac{{2x + 3}}{26} = (41)/(4)\n\n⇒ (2x + 3) = (41 × 26)/4\n\n⇒ 2x + 3 = 266.5\n\n⇒ 2x = 266.5 - 3\n\n⇒ 2x = 263.5\n\n⇒ x = 263.5/2\n\n⇒ x = 131.75\n\n∴ The value of x is 131.75.\n\ne5:T810",
